{"id":"custom","question":"¿Por qué el cielo es azul?","answers":[],"need":null,"passes":[{"stop":0,"gen":67,"calls":0,"err":""}],"raw":"The sky appears blue because of a phenomenon called Rayleigh scattering. Sunlight travels through the Earth's atmosphere and interacts with molecules and small particles. Blue light waves are scattered more than other colors because they travel in shorter, smaller waves. This scattered blue light reaches our eyes from all directions, making the sky look blue during the day."}
{"id":"custom","question":"Warum ist der Himmel blau?","answers":[],"need":null,"passes":[{"stop":0,"gen":91,"calls":0,"err":""}],"raw":"Der Himmel erscheint blau, weil Sonnenlicht in der Atmosphäre der Erde durch eine Wirkung namens Rayleigh-Streuung verteilt wird. Kürzere Wellenlängen, wie Blau und Violet, werden stärker gestreut als längere Wellenlängen wie Rot. Dadurch erreichen unsere Augen das Licht, das in blauem Spektrum liegt, und wir wahrnehmen den Himmel als blau."}
